Three MLP models are trained with identical architecture but different random initialisations. Predictions are aggregated as the mean softmax output across all three models, and uncertainty is the normalised predictive entropy of the ensemble mean. Independent initialisations encourage functional diversity among ensemble members, so disagreement between members reflects genuine ambiguity rather than single-model noise.

