We applied paired Wilcoxon signed-rank tests [] to fold-level accuracies. The signed-rank test is appropriate here because it makes no distributional assumptions about fold-level accuracy, which is bounded and asymmetrically distributed. All comparisons were two-sided. For 1D-CNN and TCN comparisons, the test was applied across the 17 sampled folds, with the baseline methods aligned to the same fold indices. Holm correction [] was applied to control the family-wise error rate across the eight pre-specified pairwise comparisons; the correction was computed programmatically within the analysis pipeline.

