Reliability diagrams are shown in Fig. . The deterministic MLP softmax is well-calibrated in the mid-range confidence bins. MC Dropout is systematically underconfident across all bins, and Deep Ensembles exhibit moderate underconfidence. EDL produces a degenerate calibration diagram: virtually all predictions are assigned to the [0.8, 1.0] confidence bin regardless of correctness, confirming vacuity collapse.

Figure  shows per-subject mean uncertainty plotted against LOSOCV accuracy for each UQ method. MC Dropout exhibits a weak negative correlation (r=-0.142): subjects with higher mean predictive entropy tend to have marginally lower LOSOCV accuracy, but the relationship is not strong enough to serve as a reliable pre-deployment screening tool. Deep Ensembles show an identical correlation (r=-0.142). EDL shows effectively no correlation (r=0.043), consistent with its uninformative confidence scores.

