This Boolean was used in a search of three journal databases: Web of Science, PsycInfo, and PsycArticles. Topic search (TS), which includes title, keywords, and abstracts in the search, was used on Web of Science. Abstract search (AB) was used in PsycArticles and PsycInfo, as there was no topic search functionality in these databases. Publication years were set from January 1, 2014, to December 31, 2025. The subject limitation of “SU = Psychology” was removed in the PsycArticles and PsycInfo search, as its inclusion greatly reduced the number of articles found, and this database is already limited to the subject area of psychology. Web of Science (4,092), PsychInfo (2,370), and PsycArticles (113) together returned 6,575 total papers, which were automatically screened using EndNote 20, with 774 automatically removed for not being articles and another 629 automatically removed for being duplicates. In total, 5,172 articles were hand-reviewed, of which a further 170 were duplicates (which were not detected earlier due to slight differences in the automatically retrieved abstracts), 274 were not peer-reviewed articles, and 18 were retracted. Furthermore, 202 retrieved documents did not contain an abstract, and these were manually found through journal searches, where only 19 were found to be journal articles and included in the review.

Two reviewers (TCW and AMG) independently conducted a review of titles and abstracts using the exclusion criteria detailed in Table . Papers that were not available in English were also excluded. Any papers for which a reviewer was listed as an author were only reviewed by the other reviewer. In this phase, very high inter-rater reliability (k = 0.77) was achieved, with 545 retained papers and 270 disagreements. In cases of disagreement, after reviewer discussion, a further 169 articles were retained, and a total of 714 articles proceeded to full-text review (Fig. ).
