The full text of each article was downloaded and read, with multi-study papers separated into individual studies. A hand-search was conducted by a single reviewer (TCW) to extract the stimuli source (e.g., fact-checking websites or researcher-created), stimuli number (true and fake news), piloted pre-ratings (e.g., controlling for emotionality or plausibility), and stimuli framing (e.g., presented as a Facebook article or a plain text headline), and example or full set availability. These data were extracted into a Microsoft Excel document, which is available at https://osf.io/bqac5/?view_only=e8a7d8c177104bec9da7d6899c8b6678.

