To determine the most frequently used topics in psychological fake news research, the topic areas of fake news within the studies were extracted. Topics were coded by one reviewer based on the topics explicitly stated in-text, or were extracted from the full stimuli set if no topic was specified in-text. Extracted text indicating the topic of news stimuli are detailed in the OSF extraction spreadsheet. The topics of the fake news articles used are detailed in Table . In 563 studies (63.9%), the fake news stories were intentionally constrained to one news area (a single topic), such as political events, COVID-19, or health. Overall, 146 studies (16.6%) categorized their news into two or three topics, while 162 studies (18.4%) had many different topics (more than four, or one topic per stimuli). Some studies did not specify the topic of their news (18 studies, 2.0%). The most frequently researched topic was political news (273 studies, 31.0%).
