To assess the transparency and replicability of fake news stimuli in research, any note or explanation in-text of example fake news stimuli or where to find them was extracted. In this case, the example had to align with the stimuli framing, so an example of a generic web news story had to have shown an example of image and headline (see previous section for specific content details). Most studies provided examples either in the text (550 studies, 62.4%) or in an appendix or supplemental material (244 studies, 27.7%), with a total of 794 studies (90.1%) showing an accessible example. Only 57 studies (6.5%) did not provide examples, or examples were specifically mentioned as request-only by the authors. Lastly, 29 studies (3.3%) only showed partial examples (see the Note for Table  for an explanation of partial examples).
